The most common calls to tamedog() (scroll of taming, spell of charm
monster, magic harp) are guarded by a resist() check. Some aren't: of
these, the "charismatic" magic trap case is the only one that has
general application to an arbitrary monster.

(In the particular case under discussion, the blessed Book of the
Dead would work as well, since an arch-lich is undead; at least, it'd
get as far as making it peaceful, if it weren't already.)

